  Every page worth putting in front of a search engine, and no more.

  These are real addresses now rather than hash routes, which is what makes
  the list possible: until the Worker started serving /about and
  /collections/lvt as documents of their own (worker-pages.js), all nine of
  them were the same URL with a bookmark on the end and listing them would
  have been listing "/" nine times.

  Deliberately absent:
    /favourites  whatever this browser saved — different for everyone
    /visualiser  a tool, not a page about anything
    /collections/<type>/<style>  a filtered view of its type page, and it says
                 so in its canonical
    /range/<id>  real pages, still noindex until the Worker can name them —
                 see worker-pages.js
    /admin       behind a sign-in, and in robots.txt as well

  The old Wix URLs are not here either. They are 301s; a sitemap is for the
  destination, never the redirect.
-->
